21	+`PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_PLACEMENT=1` is a test-only setting, off by default: the dev and test entry point (`npm run dev`, and the server the browser tests start) then serves `POST /__test/place`, which puts a player's ship on a chosen tile. `PIRATE_SEA_RACE_TEST_SOURCES` (for example `sun,sun|moon,moon|sun,sun|moon,moon`, each island's source types) is another, off by default: every match then deals its rubbings in that layout instead of the private shuffle. The production entry (`npm start`) reads neither.
22	+
23	+The integration tests run in two groups (`npm run test:integration`): most files in parallel worker processes, with test-only shorter timings, then the netcode harness files (`duelHarness`, `seaDuelHarness`, `devLatency`) one after another on a quiet machine.
